title: Building Programs

files:
  - .assets/img-103-02-01.png
  - .assets/img-103-02-02.png

steps:
  - cmds:
      - view 1
    text: |
      {[ht,$start]&thinsp;Building Programs}

      This tour will focus on building **EMS** programs &ndash; and the special role played by {[cu]BuildC} within this process.

      To that end, we'll dive into a virtually empty {[cu]Gist00} pro&shy;gram targeting an absolutely minimal **EMS** distro.

      For now, go ahead and build the program as follows:

      {[DC,1]} select {[em]Board &ndash; &lt;bare-metal&gt;}<br>
      {[DC,2]} select {[em]Setup &ndash; segger.arm.sandbox://default}<br>
      {[DC,3]} locate `segger.arm.gists.sandbox/Gist00.em.ts`<br>
      {[DC,4]} click the **Build&thinsp;+&thinsp;Load** button and track progress<br>

      The **OUTPUT** panel shows status of the **EMS** translator {[dc,5]}, the backend C++ compiler {[dc,6]}, and the program loader {[dc,7]}.

      <div class="em-info">

      {[cu]Gist00} weighs in at just 156 bytes &ndash; truly tiny code&thinsp;!!

      </div>

  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,$build]&thinsp;Generated C++ Project}

  - cmds:
    text: |
      {[ht,$extra]&thinsp;Extra Credit}

  - cmds:
